meta {
  name: 44 Trigger 4 - Publish Report
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{nlabReportId}}/publish
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  ▶ Fires `lab-report.published` → lab_order_report_published_inform_patient
    ("Lab Report Completed"). AND, if this is the LAST report on the order to be
    published, ALSO fires lab_order_completed_inform_patient ("Lab Order
    Completed") — i.e. this single request can cover BOTH scenarios 4 and 5.

  PREREQUISITE: {{nlabReportId}} must be a report that has reached APPROVED (the
  publish transition is results → save → submit → validate → approve → publish).
  If publish returns a state error, approve it first:
      POST {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{nlabReportId}}/approve
  and, if needed, the earlier transitions (save/submit/validate) — those require
  entered result values (PATCH /lab-reports/:id/results) and are data-specific,
  so run them in the app/technician UI or add them here for your test order.

  To fire "Lab Order Completed" (scenario 5) explicitly, publish EVERY report on
  the order — the completion notification fires once, when the last one flips to
  PUBLISHED.
}
